<article class="env-lemma" id="0AEZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AEZ">Lemma <span data-tag="0AEZ">81.10.8</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0AEV" data-tag="0AEV">81.10.6</a>. Let $X' \to X$ be a flat morphism of algebraic spaces. Set $Z' = X' \times _ X Z$ and $Y' = X' \times _ X Y$. The pullbacks $\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X) \to \mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_{X'})$ and $\mathit{QCoh}(Y \to X, Z) \to \mathit{QCoh}(Y' \to X', Z')$ are compatible with the functors (<a href="/tag/0AEX" data-tag="0AEX">81.10.6.2</a>) and <a href="/tag/0AEW" data-tag="0AEW">81.10.6.1</a>). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because pullback commutes with pullback and because flat pullback commutes with pushforward along quasi-compact and quasi-separated morphisms, see Cohomology of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/073K" data-tag="073K">69.11.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>